# *.gz is deliberately NOT blanket-ignored: it is not a data allow-list, it just
# means a .gz somewhere else in the tree is not silently dropped.

# --- demo input data: NOT TRACKED --------------------------------------------
# Reversed 2026-08-11 (standards Rule 17.1: commit source only, never data).
# 39 real GEO files were tracked here — barcodes/genes .tsv.gz for GSE212966 and
# GSE283500 plus metadata. Two problems:
#
#   * It is research data in a source repository, and 489 MB of it on disk.
#   * The tracked copy was never usable anyway: matrix.mtx.gz is blanket-ignored
#     by the *.mtx.gz rule above, so the committed demo was missing the actual
#     count matrices. Anyone cloning got features and barcodes and no data.
#
# The accessions are recorded in README.md; download them from GEO into this
# folder to run the demo. Keep the folder, not its contents.
input_data/*
!input_data/.gitkeep

# --- bundled CellTypist models (54 MB, 41 .pkl): NOT TRACKED -----------------
# Reversed again 2026-08-11 (standards Rule 17.3: never commit a file over ~5 MB;
# Rule 16.3: never load a pickle you cannot verify).
#
#   6.2 MB   largest model (Cells_Fetal_Lung.pkl) — over the 5 MB ceiling
#   54 MB    all 41 models together, paid by every clone
#
# The previous rationale for tracking them was that a `git clone` otherwise
# shipped without them and the CellTypist voter silently downloaded all 41 on
# first run. That problem is real, and it is now solved properly rather than by
# committing binaries:
#
#   scripts/fetch_celltypist_models.py   fetches every model in the manifest and
#                                        verifies each SHA-256 before it is kept
#   celltype_consensus/model_integrity.py verifies again at load time, so a
#                                        corrupt or swapped pickle raises instead
#                                        of being unpickled
#
# The two small TEXT files stay tracked, because they are what makes the download
# verifiable and reproducible: models.json (upstream URLs) and SHA256SUMS.txt
# (expected digest + size per model). Both are excluded from the blanket ignores
# by being .txt/.json, so no negation is needed for them.

# --- note on the marker library ---------------------------------------------
# Pruned 2026-08-06 from 2,075 files (25 MB) to the 4 that matter, after grepping
# every read_csv/read_excel/open/glob in the tree. Pruned again 2026-08-07 to 2,
# dropping the demo-only disease markers. What remains under
# single_cell_pipeline_agent_datasets/ and why:
#
#   TIS_CELL_markers_v3/master_celltype_markers_long.csv   read every run
#                                                          (lineage_panels.py:79)
#   its README.md                                          data provenance
#
# Deleted: cell_markers_db_2.0/, human_azimuth_reference_csvs/, panglo_db/,
# celltype_markers_top50/, subtype_ref/, the unread remainder of
# TIS_CELL_markers_v3/, and all of Disease_specific_markers/ — the squamous-cell
# CSV was read only by tests/annotation_reference_demo.py, which nothing calls.
# All of it is still in the repo-root Celltype_Markers_References/ library if it
# is ever needed again.
# Nothing above is git-ignored — both files are small and MUST stay tracked.

# PubMed retrieval cache (regenerated on demand, keyed by query hash).
# BOTH spellings are real: run_pubmed_annotation() writes <out_dir>/_pubmed_cache,
# while PubMedAnnotationConfig's own default is a CWD-relative .pubmed_cache, which
# is what you get when a script or notebook builds the config directly.
_pubmed_cache/
.pubmed_cache/

# benchmark run artifacts (regenerated by tests/benchmarks/run_benchmarks.py)
tests/benchmarks/outputs/
tests/benchmarks/logs/
tests/benchmarks/benchmark_results.json
tests/benchmarks/BENCHMARK_REPORT.md

# Annotation-benchmark result tables (regenerated by
# benchmarks/run_annotation_benchmark.py). The HARNESS is tracked; its outputs are
# not — they are derived from an .h5ad plus a seed, both recorded in each run's
# manifest.json. Archive the results directory with the paper's data deposit, not
# in git.
benchmarks/results/

# LLM response cache (llm_cache.py). Content-addressed by a hash of the full
# request, so it is regenerable but NOT reproducible-by-recomputation: replaying it
# is the whole point. Left untracked because it grows per cohort, but it is a
# REQUIRED artifact of any published run — archive it alongside the results so a
# reader can regenerate the labels offline with no API key. See
# benchmarks/README.md.
.llm_cache/

# ============================================================================
# Unused / irrelevant to the code — verified 2026-08-07 by grepping every
# read_csv/read_excel/open/glob/import in cellcyrix/, tests/ and main.py.
# shared_reference/ is deliberately NOT touched here: it IS read every run
# (lineage_panels.py resolves the TIS_CELL table and the 41 CellTypist models
# out of it) and its negations above must keep working.
# ============================================================================

# Duplicate of the code now living at the repo root. `diff -rq` shows the shared
# files are byte-identical; keeping both would publish the same package twice.
single_cell_pipeline_agent_standalone/

# 30 MB / 2,106 files, and the code never reads it. lineage_panels.py:117 lists
# it only as a LEGACY fallback that never fires — tis_cell_marker_table()
# resolves to shared_reference/ first. The only other mention is
# tests/annotation_reference_demo.py, which nothing calls.
#
# ANCHORED to the repo root, and this matters. Written unanchored, this pattern
# matched at ANY depth — and because core.ignorecase is true on Windows it also
# caught shared_reference/single_cell_pipeline_agent_datasets/
# celltype_markers_references/, excluding the 1.2 MB TIS_CELL marker table that
# lineage_panels.py reads on EVERY run. The comment above line 152 asserts that
# table "MUST stay tracked"; a later unanchored rule silently overrode it, so a
# fresh clone had no marker panels and the lineage gate fell back to its built-in
# ones. The leading slash restricts the rule to the repo-root library it was
# written for.
/Celltype_Markers_References/

# Internal planning tracker — not code, not read by anything.
BiRAGAS_One_Week_Execution_Tracker*.xlsx

# Captured CLI output from a manual run.
test_run_cli.txt

# --- docs/: prose stays tracked, generated binaries do not -------------------
# No file under docs/ is read by the pipeline. The .md documentation is worth
# versioning; the decks, spreadsheets and rendered PNGs are regenerated
# artifacts that bloat the history. Remove a line here to publish one.
docs/*.pptx
docs/*.xlsx
docs/*.png
docs/figures/
docs/Module-linkage/

# Bundled external repo — a separate superset project (bulk cohort DE + CAR-T),
# not this pipeline's code. Was ignored before the root .gitignore was replaced;
# restored here so it does not get published from this repo.
Oncocyrix_MultiCohort-master/
